# Netlify headers — awkale.me
#
# This file MUST end up in the publish directory (build/client) to take effect.
# Vite copies public/* to the output root, which is why it lives in public/ and
# not at the repo root. A root-level _headers is silently ignored.

# --- staging guard: REMOVE AT CUTOVER ----------------------------------------
#
# ADR-0002 puts the new site on a public *.netlify.app while awkale.me still
# serves the old one, and chose a sitewide noindex over password protection — the
# project has no password set, so this is the only thing stopping a staging copy
# of the whole archive being indexed as a duplicate of the real site.
#
# Delete this block at cutover, in the same change that adds the ALIAS. Leaving it
# in place ships a site nobody can find.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# --- /contact/sent/ : noindex, permanently ------------------------------------
#
# ADR-0011. A real prerendered page with no inbound purpose — it exists only because
# a native POST has to land somewhere. It must never be indexed.
#
# THIS RULE IS CURRENTLY REDUNDANT AND MUST NOT BE DELETED FOR THAT REASON. The
# sitewide staging block above covers it incidentally today; removing that block at
# cutover is precisely what exposes this page. Landing the rule first, while it is
# still a no-op, is the only way it cannot be forgotten in the same edit that makes
# it necessary — which is the coupling AWK-44 exists to manage.
#
# Both spellings are listed deliberately. Netlify normalises trailing slashes when
# matching REDIRECTS; it is not documented as doing so for HEADERS, and the served
# canonical form here is slash-ful while the prerender enumerator is slash-free. Two
# lines cost nothing; a missed match costs an indexed page nobody wanted.
/contact/sent
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/contact/sent/
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# --- fonts --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self-hosted, content-hashed at build, so they can be cached hard. These are the
# latin-subset woff2 files in public/fonts — see that directory's README for the
# diacritics caveat before ADR-0007's IMSLP pass ships.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
